WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.185
Welcome to Grade 5 English, Unit 2: Exploring Space.

2
00:00:03.265 --> 00:00:09.903
Unit 2 pairs two information texts about astronomy and
life on the space station with The Burrow Discovery,

3
00:00:09.983 --> 00:00:12.163
a story about a school science fair.

4
00:00:12.243 --> 00:00:17.752
Learners study twenty-five words such as
burrow, boycott, glare, cooperate and ownership,

5
00:00:17.832 --> 00:00:22.649
and they master indefinite pronouns,
singular agreement and adverbial phrases.

6
00:00:22.729 --> 00:00:29.869
They separate fact from opinion, compare biography with
autobiography, and write a friendly blog post of their own.

7
00:00:29.949 --> 00:00:35.144
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

8
00:00:35.224 --> 00:00:41.729
By the end of this unit, you will be able to
use the twenty-five Unit 2 words about science,

9
00:00:41.809 --> 00:00:45.953
systems and social values accurately in speech and writing.

10
00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:53.684
You will also identify indefinite pronouns in a text
and use them with the matching singular or plural verb.

11
00:00:53.764 --> 00:01:00.914
You will also read an information text about astronomy
and extract main points supported by evidence.

12
00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:03.563
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:03.643 --> 00:01:09.523
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
independence, issue, empire, expose, glare, source.

14
00:01:09.603 --> 00:01:14.501
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:14.581 --> 00:01:18.372
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:18.452 --> 00:01:23.550
The reading sequence includes The Night
Sky Above Us and Life on the Space Station.

17
00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:24.423
Read actively.

18
00:01:24.503 --> 00:01:28.727
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:28.807 --> 00:01:32.782
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:32.862 --> 00:01:38.853
The first language focus is Indefinite pronouns:
talking about people and things in general.

21
00:01:38.933 --> 00:01:44.858
Indefinite pronouns stand in for people or
things when we do not need to name them exactly.

22
00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:50.006
One short word can replace a whole list,
which keeps writing smooth and clear.

23
00:01:50.086 --> 00:01:57.198
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:01:57.278 --> 00:02:01.629
In speaking, you will complete Speaking
1: Astronaut interview role-play.

25
00:02:01.709 --> 00:02:05.696
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:02:05.776 --> 00:02:08.791
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:08.871 --> 00:02:12.008
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:12.088 --> 00:02:13.581
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:13.661 --> 00:02:20.350
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:23.632
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:23.712 --> 00:02:31.221
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
